From b8ee4e499e8127f4d7a638add2fe91fa3ac80a92 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: arena-agent <agent@arena.ai>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 05:45:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(deps): make npm ci resolve and the app build
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

npm ci fails on main with ERESOLVE, so every CI job stops at the install step
and the app cannot be started — or deployed — from a clean checkout:

    npm error Conflicting peer dependency: eslint@9.39.5
    npm error peer eslint@"^7.23.0 || ^8.0.0 || ^9.0.0" from eslint-config-next@15.5.25
    npm error     dev eslint@"^10.10.0" from the root project

eslint 10 is ahead of what eslint-config-next 15 declares. Pinned to ^9.39.5,
which satisfies the peer range Next 15 supports.

Tailwind was pinned to ^4.3.3 while the project is authored for v3: globals.css
uses the @tailwind directives and tailwind.config.ts uses the v3 content/darkMode
API, so postcss.config.mjs (tailwindcss + autoprefixer) fails at build time with
"trying to use tailwindcss directly as a PostCSS plugin". A host like Vercel or
Netlify therefore cannot build this repo at all. Pinned to ^3.4.19, matching the
config files as written; moving to v4 is a separate migration.

Lockfile regenerated so npm ci passes.
