Adds the hosting configuration the deployment section only described in prose.

* vercel.json — pins `npm ci` and `npm run build` for Vercel.
* netlify.toml — selects the Next.js runtime (@netlify/plugin-nextjs); a static
  publish cannot work because search, feeds, sitemap, reporting and caching are
  server-rendered by design.
* README — official Deploy buttons for both hosts, plus the site-URL order.

Site URLs now resolve at deploy time instead of forcing dashboard setup:

  1. NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL  (explicit override, any host)
  2. VERCEL_URL            (Vercel, both set during builds)
  3. DEPLOY_PRIME_URL, URL (Netlify)
  4. http://localhost:3000 (local development)

A first deploy without any environment variables therefore emits correct
canonical URLs, Open Graph tags, sitemap.xml and robots.txt. resolveSiteUrl also
adds the missing scheme to Vercel's scheme-less host, and keeps the empty string
meaningful for NEXT_PUBLIC_OMNISOURCE_API_URL (empty = bundled feed).

Adds 6 tests covering the resolution order.
